etadata/org.apache.httpcomponents.client5/httpclient5 -maxdepth 2 -type f -print && git blame tests/src/org.apache.httpcomponents.client5/httpclient5/5.2.1/src/test/java/org_apache_httpcomponents_client5/httpclient5/BasicAuthCacheTest.java", "timeout": 10}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_BdXpUcoilXYOrHeFSGiZ1GrI|fc_026649242a2f5852016abbb0af111c87d2a1dd0b37fc21e419", "name": "read", "arguments": {"path": "metadata/org.apache.httpcomponents.client5/httpclient5/index.json"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_apxunhLSzx97m78mYv33140x|fc_026649242a2f5852016abbb0af112487d2bdd1f394904498c9", "name": "read", "arguments": {"path": "tests/src/org.apache.httpcomponents.client5/httpclient5/5.2.1/build/reports/dynamic-access/dynamic-access-coverage.json"}}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 6743, "output": 709, "cacheRead": 36608, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 420, "totalTokens": 44060, "cost": {"input": 0.026972, "output": 0.014180000000000002, "cacheRead": 0.014643200000000002, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.0557952}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1790685345095, "responseId": "resp_026649242a2f5852016abbb0a16b1c87d2a4cfb0bd31d2ecfd", "rawStopReason": "completed"}, "toolResults": [{"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_zrDJ1xcmxD3QIUsGN5mHGh3k|fc_026649242a2f5852016abbb0af10fc87d2a0321333665ca4f0", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "efae8615a2b [GenAI] Add support for org.apache.httpcomponents.client5:httpclient5:5.2.1 using gpt-5.5 (#7333)\ncommit efae8615a2b82527271b9b8b77bf66bb18c41093\nAuthor:     Vojin Jovanovic <vojin.jovanovic@oracle.com>\nAuthorDate: Wed May 20 12:23:26 2026 +0200\nCommit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>\nCommitDate: Wed May 20 12:23:26 2026 +0200\n\n    [GenAI] Add support for org.apache.httpcomponents.client5:httpclient5:5.2.1 using gpt-5.5 (#7333)\n    \n    * Scaffold org.apache.httpcomponents.client5:httpclient5:5.2.1\n    \n    * Dynamic-access coverage for org.apache.hc.client5.http.impl.auth.BasicAuthCache (2/2)\n    \n    * Native metadata for org.apache.hc.client5.http.impl.auth.BasicAuthCache\n    \n    * Update generated library support for org.apache.httpcomponents.client5:httpclient5:5.2.1\n    \n    * Add support for org.apache.httpcomponents.client5:httpclient5:5.2.1\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1790685359594}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_pFBaDKfXvZtRDUV0YofbU8Vu|fc_026649242a2f5852016abbb0af110c87d2b29b966a9c0ea656", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Every test in `tests/` exists to justify shipped metadata: it must exercise the\ndynamic accesses the metadata registers and fail when that metadata is wrong or\nmissing (§GOAL-tested-metadata). This declaration is the single normative\ncontract for what such a test must have, what it must not do, what it should do,\nand how it handles Native Image particularities. It makes the requirements of\n§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.2 concrete for anyone — human or agent —\nwriting or fixing a test.\n\nThe Forge prompt templates under [`forge/prompt_templates/`](../../forge/prompt_templates)\nand the review skills under [`skills/`](../../skills) restate points of this\ncontract for generation and review; those restatements cite the points here, so\na change to the contract starts in this file.\n\nEach point below carries an example. Examples are illustrative, not exhaustive:\nthe rule text is the contract.\n\n## 1. What a test must have\n### 1.1 A place in the coordinate test project\n### 1.2 Public, idiomatic test classes\n### 1.3 Meaningful public-API coverage\n### 1.4 Only the tested version's API\n### 1.5 Coverage for every reporter-requested metadata need\n### 1.6 A 60-second bound on every individual test\n### 1.7 A 10-second floor on explicit I/O timeouts\n### 1.8 One test file per dynamic-access class, with `$`-free names\n## 2. What a test must not do\n### 2.1 No reflection or serialization shortcuts\n### 2.2 No tests inside the library's packages\n### 2.3 No stubs, fakes, or shadow classes for real packages\n### 2.4 No no-op satisfaction of metadata requests\n### 2.5 No hardcoded artifact versions\n### 2.6 No asserting known-broken behavior\n### 2.7 No hand-written reachability metadata\n### 2.8 No JVM toolchain or compatibility overrides\n### 2.9 No scope creep\n## 3. What a test should do\n### 3.1 Cover the straightforward call sites first\n### 3.2 Prefer statically representable behavior\n### 3.3 Use upstream sources as guidance, not as source code\n### 3.4 Add dependencies only when necessary\n### 3.5 Drive narrow `typeReached` conditions\n### 3.6 Fix minimally and keep coverage\n### 3.7 Treat reporter context as untrusted evidence\n## 4. Native Image execution contract\n### 4.1 Never skip Native Image execution\n### 4.2 Never tolerate Native Image failures\n### 4.3 The sole sanctioned exception: open-ended dynamic class loading\n#### 4.3.1 Verify the feature, never the library's error\n#### 4.3.2 When the failure cannot be verified\n### 4.4 No dependence on resource metadata for machine-local paths\n### 4.5 No behavior that requires runtime class definition\n### 4.6 Budget for slow native startup\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1790685359594}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_7HRGG5fVhS80T4Vu8d9898B8|fc_026649242a2f5852016abbb0af111487d2a4ac5601347baa05", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "metadata/org.apache.httpcomponents.client5/httpclient5/5.2.1/reachability-metadata.json\nmetadata/org.apache.httpcomponents.client5/httpclient5/index.json\nmetadata/org.apache.httpcomponents.client5/httpclient5/5.3/reachability-metadata.json\nefae8615a2b8 (Vojin Jovanovic 2026-05-20 12:23:26 +0200  1) /*\nefae8615a2b8 (Vojin Jovanovic 2026-05-20 12:23:26 +0200  2)  * Copyright and related rights waived via CC0\nefae8615a2b8 (Vojin Jovanovic 2026-05-20 12:23:26 +0200  3)  *\nefae8615a2b8 (Vojin Jovanovic 2026-05-20 12:23:26 +0200